reation_policy":"all","topics":["amqp","python","python-library","python3","queue-tasks","queue-workers","queued-jobs","redis","redis-queue","sqs","sqs-queue","task-manager","task-runner","task-scheduler"],"visibility":"public","forks":4989,"open_issues":773,"watchers":28268,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/pulls/9247","html_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery/pull/9247","diff_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery/pull/9247.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery/pull/9247.patch","merged_at":"2024-09-13T09:17:00Z"},"body":"## Description\r\nFixes #9119 (or tries to)\r\n\r\nThis approach assumes we want to do the dispatch_uid calculation for the user behind the scenes, and that we want to handle both the decorator and non-decorator usecases for `signal.connect(receiver, sender=sender, retry=True)`\r\n\r\nNotes:\r\n- edited _make_lookup_key instead of _make_id, doesn't seem to be much of a difference, but I wanted the change as far up the stack as possible so devs can see it sooner\r\n- we can potentially also use functools.wraps and `__wrapped__` (i.e., `functools.wraps(fun)(retry_over_time)` in decorator form), but this is a bit too generic for this type of solution, which may cause other issues\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/9247/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/9247/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/comments/2339375775","html_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery/issues/9119#issuecomment-2339375775","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/9119","id":2339375775,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAALQjM6LcAqf","user":{"login":"pachewise","id":2257119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTcxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2257119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachewise","html_url":"https://github.com/pachewise","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachewise/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachewise/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachewise/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachewise/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachewise/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachewise/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachewise/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachewise/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachewise/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-10T00:21:58Z","updated_at":"2024-09-10T00:24:53Z","body":"I opened a [small PR](https://github.com/celery/celery/pull/9247), but need some guidance as to whether this approach is desirable or not. IMO, if we are supporting both the decorator and non-decorator usecases, then we need a way to tell `disconnect()` to compare the uid to the original function's. Another thing we can do is to simply use the uid for the retry-wrapped function (implicitly, `_make_id(_retry_receiver(fun))`), but that seems to break the original retry tests in test_dispatcher.py","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/comments/2339375775/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"pachewise","id":2257119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTcxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2257119?v=4","gravatar_id":"",